{'symbol': 'MS', 'date': '2020-01-16 10:30:00', 'title': 'Morgan Stanley Reports Q4 Adjusted EPS Of $1.20', 'text': 'FOURTH QUARTER AND FULL YEAR 2019 EARNINGS RESULTS.Q4 NET REVENUES OF $10.9 BILLION AND EPS OF $1.30.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.99, REVENUE VIEW $9.72 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q4 OF 2019 WAS ALSO IMPACTED BY SEVERANCE COSTS OF $172 MILLION ASSOCIATED WITH A DECEMBER EMPLOYEE ACTION.CURRENT QUARTER INCLUDED AN INTERMITTENT NET DISCRETE TAX BENEFIT OF $158 MILLION OR $0.10 PER DILUTED SHARE.QTRLY ROE WAS 11.3% VERSUS 11.2% REPORTED AT Q3-END.QTRLY ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.20.QTRLY INSTITUTIONAL SECURITIES NET REVENUE $5,054 MILLION VERSUS $3,839 MILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.AS OF DEC 31, 2019 TANGIBLE BOOK VALUE PER COMMON SHARE WAS $40.01  VERSUS $39.73 AS OF SEPT 30, 2019.QTRLY WEALTH MANAGEMENT NET REVENUE $4,582 MILLION VERSUS $4,144 MILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.QTRLY INVESTMENT MANAGEMENT NET REVENUE $1,356  MILLION VERSUS $684 MILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.CEO SAYS DELIVERED STRONG QUARTERLY EARNINGS ACROSS ALL OF OUR BUSINESSES IN QUARTER.QTRLY COMPENSATION EXPENSE $5.23 BILLION VERSUS $3.79 BILLION.QTRLY EQUITY SALES AND TRADING REVENUE DECREASED IN ENVIRONMENT CHARACTERIZED BY LOWER CASH MARKET VOLUMES, LOWER VOLATILITY IN DERIVATIVES.QTRLY FIXED INCOME SALES AND TRADING REVENUE INCREASED 11% ON STRONG CLIENT ENGAGEMENT.QTRLY NON-COMPENSATION EXPENSES $2.9 BILLION VERSUS $2.9 BILLION.QTRLY SALES AND TRADING REVENUE $3,194 MILLION VERSUS $2,487 MILLION.QTRLY TRADING REVENUES $2.31 BILLION VERSUS $1.74 BILLION.'}
