{'symbol': 'PPG', 'date': '2020-01-16 11:30:00', 'title': 'PPG Reports Fourth-Quarter Earnings Per Share Of $1.23 From Continuing Operations', 'text': 'PPG REPORTS FOURTH QUARTER AND FULL-YEAR 2019 FINANCIAL RESULTS.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.23 FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.34 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.32 TO $1.42 FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.53 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.ADJUSTED Q4 EARNINGS PER DILUTED SHARE FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS OF $1.31.PPG INDUSTRIES - Q4 NET SALES OF NEARLY $3.7 BILLION, APPROXIMATELY 1% HIGHER THAN PRIOR YEAR AND UP ABOUT 2% IN CONSTANT CURRENCIES.Q4 REVENUE VIEW $3.69 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FULL-YEAR 2020 SALES GROWTH OF 1 TO 3 PERCENT IN CONSTANT CURRENCIES, INCLUDING RECENTLY ANNOUNCED ACQUISITIONS.SEES FULL-YEAR 2020 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE GROWTH OF 4% TO 9%, EXCLUDING CURRENCY TRANSLATION IMPACTS.UNFAVORABLE FOREIGN CURRENCY TRANSLATION IMPACTED NET SALES BY APPROXIMATELY 1% IN QUARTER.AS QUARTER PROGRESSED, INDUSTRIAL DEMAND BEGAN TO STABILIZE IN CHINA, BUT REMAINED CHALLENGED IN EUROPE AND U.S..WITH RESPECT TO INDUSTRIAL COATINGS SEGMENT, WE ANTICIPATE A RETURN TO VOLUME GROWTH IN SECOND HALF OF 2020.PPG INDUSTRIES - PERFORMANCE COATINGS SEGMENT SALES WILL BE IMPACTED DUE TO LOWER PRODUCTION RATES BY AN AEROSPACE CUSTOMER IN 2020.AS WE START 2020, WE EXPECT ORGANIC GROWTH IN OUR PERFORMANCE COATINGS SEGMENT TO CONTINUE.Q4 COST SAVINGS, RELATED TO RESTRUCTURING INITIATIVES, OF SLIGHTLY MORE THAN $20 MILLION AND ABOUT $85 MILLION FOR FULL-YEAR 2019.'}
